How to Play Armchair Easy Sudoku

Welcome to Armchair Easy Sudoku! Whether you're playing on a desktop or tapping away on your phone, here's a quick guide to everything you need to know to play and use our helpful tools.

Playing the Game

The goal is to fill the 9x9 grid so that every row, column, and 3x3 box contains the numbers 1 through 9 exactly once. Pre-filled clues have a gray background and can't be changed. Your guesses will appear in blue.

Desktop (Keyboard and Mouse)

Select a Box: Click any empty white box with your mouse, or use the Arrow Keys to move your selection around the grid.

Enter a Number: Type a number from 1 to 9 on your keyboard.

Delete a Number: Press Backspace or Delete on your keyboard to clear the current box.

Mobile (Touchscreen)

Select a Box: Tap any empty white box on the grid to highlight it.

Enter a Number: Tap the numbers 1 through 9 on the on-screen number pad below the grid.

Delete a Number: Tap the Delete icon (the button with the backspace symbol) on the on-screen number pad.

Special Tools

The "Notes" Feature

If you aren't sure which number belongs in a box, you can leave a small "pencil mark" or note to keep track of your possibilities.

To Turn On: Click or tap the Notes: Off button to turn it On. You can also press the 'N' key on your keyboard.

To Use: While Notes are turned on, entering a number will place a tiny number in the corner of the box instead of a large main guess. You can put multiple notes in a single box. To remove a note, just enter that same number again.

The "Swap" Feature

Quickly change a guess into a note, or promote a note to your final guess!

How to use it: Select a box and tap the Swap button (or press the Spacebar or 'S' on your keyboard).

If the box has a Main Number: It will shrink down and become a tiny Note.

If the box has exactly ONE Note: It will grow into your Main Number guess.

Game Controls

Check: Not sure if you're on the right track? Press the Check button to grade your current answers. Correct guesses will turn green, and incorrect ones will turn red.

Solve: Stuck? Pressing Solve will instantly fill in the correct solution for the entire board. Note: This will count as a "Loss" on your stats scoreboard!

New Game: Clears the board and generates a brand-new puzzle for you to solve.

Good luck, and happy solving!
